    {
      "claim": "Sulfonamide-containing drugs also meet the F>=20% threshold: celecoxib 20-40% (C07) and pazopanib 21.4% (C13); BMS-275183 24% (C22) shows that even a lower-bioavailability drug can remain above threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C07","C13","C22"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 low-permeability records for salicylic acid (C135), mefenamic acid (C162), HCTZ (C136), and sulfasalazine (C148, C155) do not establish F<20% for the query because low in vitro permeability can coexist with high oral F (diflunisal C10, meclofenamate C06, flufenamic acid C02); C178 used furosemide only as a 1 mM Caco-2 reagent and reports no furosemide Papp.",
      "card_ids": ["C135","C162","C136","C148","C155","C10","C06","C02","C178"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility/absorption records for ionized acids and sulfonamide drugs are consistent with meaningful absorption: diclofenac sodium solubility 2.43 g/L and intestinal permeability 10e-6 cm/s (C131), tamsulosin >90% absorbed (C147) and 100% absorbed (C153), and chlorothiazide solubility 3.1 mg/mL at pH 8 (C165).",
      "card_ids": ["C131","C147","C153","C165"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall efflux/intestinal-metabolism records are for other molecules (sulfasalazine, 5-ASA, salicylic acid, cromolyn, and a furfurylamino-sulfonyl analog C184) and provide no furosemide-specific efflux or intestinal-metabolism measurement; C217/C211/C214 used furosemide only as an incubation reagent in sulfasalazine transport studies. Mechanism alone is not a direct F outcome and does not overturn the high prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C217","C211","C214","C184","C193","C229","C204","C212","C215","C220","C228"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C217","C211","C214","C184","C193","C229","C204","C212","C215","C220","C228"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No furosemide-specific L5 gut-wall efflux or intestinal-metabolism record was supplied; all L5 records concern other molecules.",
    "No direct furosemide absolute F, AUC, Cmax, permeability, solubility, or fraction-absorbed record was supplied.",
    "No cystic fibrosis-specific pharmacokinetic data were supplied; extrapolation from general human and animal populations is indirect.",
    "First-pass hepatic metabolism and gut-wall extraction for the query are not directly measured.",
    "Furosemide formulation-dependent and dose-dependent absorption variability is not directly captured."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high (F>=20%). L1 direct oral-bioavailability outcomes for anthranilic acid NSAIDs and related acids are high, and sulfonamide-containing drugs meet the threshold; L4 low-permeability records for other molecules do not establish F<20% for furosemide, and L5 gut-wall efflux/intestinal-metabolism records are not furosemide-specific. The low physicochemical prior is an uncertain prior, not affirmative low-F evidence. Confidence remains moderate."
}

